      "id": 1,
      "text": "Knoxville's first courthouse, built in 1839, still stands and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knoxville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Sanburn Log Cabin, opened as a general store in 1832, now serves as a museum and is one of the town's oldest buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knoxville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every October, the Knox County Scenic Drive parade stops in Knoxville, celebrating the county's historic landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knoxville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 150‑year‑old Masonic Lodge hosts pancake breakfasts, a quirky local tradition that keeps the town’s history alive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.knoxcountyscenicdrive.com/Knoxville.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Knoxville was founded in 1831, renamed from Henderson in 1832, and became the county seat the same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knoxville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Knox County Fairgrounds, located just north of town, host the annual fair each August, drawing visitors to historic exhibits.",
